The '''Gogiida''' are an order of early echinoderms known from late Early<ref name=Durham1978>{{harvnb|Durham|1978}}</ref> to Middle Cambrian<ref name=Robinson1965>{{harvnb|Robinson|1965}}</ref> deposits.
The order is likely [[paraphyletic]] with all or some members of [[Eocrinidae]] closer to more derived eocrinoids than to [[Lyracystidae]].

The order includes the families [[Eocrinida]], which includes ''[[Eocrinus]]'', ''[[Gogia]]'' and several of their relatives, and [[Lyracystidae]], wihch contains only the genera ''[[Lyracystis]]'' and ''[[Balangicystis]]''.<ref>{{harvnb|Sprinkle|Parsley|Zhao|Peng|2011|p=253}}</ref>

